/Title (The law of property \(or law of goods\) is the branch of civil law that regulates assets and the legal relationships between people and things. In Colombia, its study begins with the primacy of the 1991 Constitution, which establishes the social and ecological character of property. The concept of assets \(patrimony\) is defined as the set of goods and rights with economic value inherent to each person. All movable or immovable goods that a person possesses form their indivisible patrimony.)
